WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.934
International Women's

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:01.534
Day, a

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.736
day to honor achievements

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.871
by women all around the world.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.439
But for women in Ukraine, it's

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.508
another day of grinding war

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.843
as Ukrainian forces

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.577
try to fend off

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.411
Russian troops

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.278
in the pivotal

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.581
eastern city of parliament.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.382
Ukrainian women

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.950
have been killed in a year

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.219
long war since Russia invaded.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:20.854
They've been wounded.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:21.688
They've lost their loved

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.289
ones, their homes

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.625
and their hope for a secure future.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.194
Ukrainian President Zelenskiy honor

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.162
the women who have given

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.897
their lives to the country

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.298
and had this message

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.768
for the Ukrainian people.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.603
Grandchildren

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.604
when you meet the

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.305
Ukrainian men and women.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.741
Today is International Women's Day,

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.611
a day of the fight for women's rights.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.280
Each year I thank my mother.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.782
I call her to thank her

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.716
that there has always been

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.084
respect in my family.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:52.752
I thank my

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.220
wife that we love each other

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.790
and that we have beautiful children.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.426
I think women who work with me.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:00.527
It is very important

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.296
that we are equal colleagues

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.832
With time now for the exchange

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.801
and joining me is in itself son.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.369
She's a member of Ukraine's parliament

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.870
and served as Ukraine's deputy

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.972
minister of education and science

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.475
from 2014 to 2016.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.843
A pleasure to have you on the show

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.211
and happy International Women's Day.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.813
Thanks for your time

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.815
Thank you for having me.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.515
And.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:25.151
Same to you and all of us.

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.153
So we obviously have been following

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:30.123
the battle for Mode for many weeks now.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.225
Ukraine obviously doing

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.160
all it can to defend that city

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.562
because the fear is that Russia,

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.196
should it take

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.898
that city, will have an open road

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.766
to take larger

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.700
industrial cities

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.769
like crematoria and Slovyansk.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.604
What can you tell us

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.473
about the battle on the front lines that.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.676
Well, the situation in

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:50.810
Bermuda is indeed

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.179
very tense and very difficult

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.881
because Russia has basically

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:56.282
put all the forces

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.451
that they could dispense of

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.453
into that very small town

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.888
Why it is so important?

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:02.522
Because, yes,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.089
they believe

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.657
that once they take over Bermuda,

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.426
they would be able to approach

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.627
big industrial zones

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.761
in Kramatorsk

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.829
where people are still live

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.764
and families are still living.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:12.999
And that is what Russians

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.701
want to get access to,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.302
because once they get there,

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.338
it would basically be able to claim that

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.673
absolute majority of Donetsk

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.708
and Luhansk regions

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:22.642
or the whole Donbass

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.911
all together is under their control.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.613
And potentially for them,

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.915
that would be at least one way to claim

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.151
some sort of victory within this

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.486
this whole year of a full scale invasion

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.621
where they don't

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.455
really have a victory

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.457
to report to their own people.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.292
That is why this battle of Bermuda became

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.561
so intensely important for them.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.662
But then there is also

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.763
a kind of internal

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.765
political dimension to that,

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.834
because the major force

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:48.668
on the Russian side

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.271
fighting is the so-called Wagner Group,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.407
which is a private military company,

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.409
which is using very,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.013
very difficult methods of warfare.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.447
They basically don't care

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.582
about the number of losses.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.284
They have lost thousands of people

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.618
in that small town,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.487
but they don't care about that.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.155
They just need to show results

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.757
because that the leader of the group

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:11.157
and Mr.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:11.958
Prigozhin,

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.959
he wants to show that he's

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.260
going to be more efficient

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.428
than the minister of defense.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.229
So there is this

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.064
internal political dimension

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.966
now on the Russian side to that.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.100
But because of that,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.735
they have put an all forces

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.070
available in Bermuda.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.172
And that is why it's very difficult

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.240
for Ukrainian forces

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.176
to hold to the town at this point.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.912
And I was just reading about the 29 year

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:33.947
old medic,

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:34.681
the paramedic

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.817
who was photographed in action in March

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.520
and days later, she lost her life.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.122
Talk to us about the impact of this

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.091
war on the women of Ukraine.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:47.994
Well, the

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.262
impact is immense,

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.064
like like on men as well.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.032
But I think it is slightly different

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:53.967
for women,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.169
and it's actually a bit of divergent

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.973
ways in how this war affected women,

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.374
because on the one hand,

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.108
of course,

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.344
multiples of women, millions of women

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.312
have been kind of streamlined

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:08.881
into various stereotypical

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.316
roles of mothers

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.051
where they had to take their kids,

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.220
grab them and move out of the country.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.623
Or if they stay inside the country,

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.524
they taken care of their kids,

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.526
became kind of their major,

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.227
major job

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:23.129
because their partners

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.331
have left for the poor, the frontline.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.166
So on the one hand, there was this,

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:27.500
you know,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.468
streamlining them

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:30.737
in those stereotypical women's roles.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:32.105
But on the other hand,

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:34.407
the truth is that also many,

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.643
many women joined Ukrainian armed forces.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.611
We have over 50,000 women

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.746
who are currently fighting

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.781
in the armed forces of Ukraine,

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.916
and they're gaining recognition.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.886
So now when we talk about our defenders

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.655
in Ukrainian language,

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.756
like, for instance, in French,

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.090
there are different

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:51.958
known forms

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.127
from male and female professions.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.362
So now when we talk about our defenders,

00:04:56.362 --> 00:05:00.033
we use both female and male nouns,

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.635
so to speak, for defender in Ukrainian

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.336
to signifies

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:04.304
that we recognize

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.805
that there are also Ukrainian women

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.907
who are actually fighting this war

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:09.876
be to us as directly as fighters

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.278
or as as military medics in whatever role

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.680
they choose to do.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.981
But but in that sense

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:15.682
they kind of

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:17.517
break in those stereotypes

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:18.017
and showing

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.452
that they can do different things,

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.120
not just to be mothers,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.822
but also being being fighters,

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:24.724
being soldiers, doing other things

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.193
So in that sense, of course,

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.262
that that's a bit of a different

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.531
way in how lives of Ukrainian women's

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.532
work change.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:34.367
And then there is the third element

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.868
so dimension to that,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:36.669
and that is, of course,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.738
the women who became direct victims

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:39.372
of Russian

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.908
aggression, women who have been killed,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.710
women who have been raped,

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.112
women who have been deported to Russia.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:47.680
They also have been separated

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.681
from their families

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:49.082
of those

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:49.916
who have been separated

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.818
from their children.

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.019
That's another dimension

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:54.187
in how women have.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:54.887
But women's lives

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.456
have changed, of course.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:59.058
And that is that is a very hard break.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.828
And that probably the most heartbreaking

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:03.463
group of women.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.932
That's very difficult to to even find

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:08.134
words, to express

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.636
all feelings.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:11.938
But I know for sure that we

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.706
have to recognize them

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:16.209
their sacrifice and

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:17.643
what they have gone through

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.644
and try to remember

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.780
this is some sacrifice they made.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:22.281
Absolutely.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.317
And interestingly,

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:25.451
Russia's war against

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.520
Ukraine is also galvanized

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.890
support for LGBTQ rights.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.125
You're one of a

00:06:32.125 --> 00:06:33.426
number of lawmakers

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.028
who has not only supported legislation

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.263
to prohibit

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.399
hate speech against that community,

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.701
but also introduce legislation

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.469
to give partnership rights

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.338
to same sex couples.

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.973
What more can you tell us?

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.574
Yes, indeed.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.475
It was yesterday

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:50.476
that I introduced

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:51.844
a bill to the parliament,

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.112
and I'm now

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.881
talking to attempts to co-sponsor

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:55.681
this bill.

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.149
And the bill

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:57.216
was basically allow

00:06:57.216 --> 00:06:59.051
for same sex couples

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:01.120
to register their partnerships,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.223
which is for me is a basic human right.

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.292
We should not tell other people

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:06.993
whom to lie

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:09.262
and how to organize their lives.

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:10.763
But it's particularly important

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:11.564
at this point of time

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.166
because we do have

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:15.368
LGBT people fighting in the Army

00:07:15.735 --> 00:07:17.170
and them not being able

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.472
to register relations with their partner

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.442
has very dire and direct consequences.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:23.042
In case

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:25.178
something happens to or to LGBT,

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:27.413
a man or woman in the front line

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:28.514
and that they need medical help.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:29.282
For instance,

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:30.616
their partner would not be able

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.385
to make medical decisions

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.886
instead of him or her

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:34.487
because

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.388
because that would not

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:36.989
be legally possible.

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:38.257
So so we need to make sure

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:39.959
that those who are protecting us

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:42.028
are protected by our society

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.729
and by our legislation.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.631
And that is the major

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:46.532
driving force

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.634
why we introduce in this legislation now,

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.570
because those who are on the frontline

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.971
need this protection

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.906
And that is why I hope the lawmakers

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:55.174
will understand this.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.275
And despite

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.543
there are conservative elements

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.278
in the society majority.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:01.614
56% of Ukrainians actually support

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.249
this type of legislation.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:03.816
And I hope

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:05.751
that this will equally be supported

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.620
by the Ukrainian parliament.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.289
And this is exactly the opposite of what

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:13.125
the Russian president Putin would want

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.060
in a solution.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.194
Thanks so much for your time.

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.229
We really appreciate it.

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.230
We wish you all the best.

00:08:18.364 --> 00:08:19.131
Thank you so much.

